From c0f55e81f037ded3df7ff37ad8109d8061c5db1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 04:42:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Stop the Voice Recorder crashing, and give it controls

MediaRecorder.prepare() throws IOException and start() throws
IllegalStateException when the microphone is held by a call or another
app. Both ran unguarded on the main thread inside the record button's
click handler, so a busy mic was a process crash rather than a failed
recording. They are wrapped now, the recorder is released on the failure
path, and the user is told what happened.

The recorder also produced whatever MediaRecorder defaulted to, with no
say from the user - against the rule that every tool producing output
lets the user control it. Three capture presets now, from a 22 kHz mono
voice note to 44 kHz stereo, with the trade spelled out on each. A clock
and a level meter make it obvious the microphone is live, the recorder is
released when the screen goes away instead of holding the mic open, and
the result goes through ToolResultCard so it can be shared as well as
saved.

Audio Joiner: joinAudio returning null used to leave the button doing
nothing at all, which reads as the app ignoring the tap - it now says
which file it could not decode. Files can be reordered and removed before
joining, which is the point of a joiner.

Audited alongside this: all 132 registry tools dispatch to a real
implementation. No file under ads/ is touched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
